d attorneys  fees and costs each side had 20 minutes  to present evidence but tasha's lawyers  who are criminal defense lawyers only  took 90 seconds the jury awarded cardi  an additional 2.8 million dollars in  punitive damages and attorneys fees  georgia allows punitive damages in  defamation cases under certain  circumstances punitive damages are given  solely to punish or penalize or deter a  defendant and to prove those damages a  plaintiff must show that the defendant's  actions showed willful misconduct malice  fraud wantedness or oppression if the  defendant demonstrated total disregard  for the consequences of her actions a  jury can impose punitive damages to  punish that defendant and a plaintiff  must prove this by clear and convincing  evidence which is higher than the  preponderance standard that you're  usually dealing with in a civil case  though there is a 250 000 cap on  punitive damages in georgia unless the  plaintiff can prove specific intent to  cause harm the jury deliberated for two  hours before deciding that cardi b had  proved that tasha intended to cause harm  now there's also some really interesting  inside baseball here involving toshike  and her lawyers  cardi b filed suit against tasha k and  tasha k also filed counter claims for  assault and iid so effectively within  the same case she sued cardi b she  asserted that cardi deliberately got her  fans riled up by falsely claiming that  tasha was stalking cardi and her friends  and making up fake stories she also said  that cardi called her names like dumbass  [ __ ] and ho tasha also said that when  cardi threatened to bankrupt tasha by  stating quote and i'm quoting here uh  all right then [ __ ] i'm gonna take all  your [ __ ] bread she meant that she  was going to get violent tasha said  cardi's fans then made verbal threats  and she was forced to move several times  because of the fans the judge dismissed  these counter claims because tasha  couldn't prove that cardi b herself had 